The legal texts come from the Congreso de la República del Perú:

  Fuente: Congreso de la República del Perú, ediciones oficiales de la Constitución Política del Perú
  (mayo de 2021 y diciembre de 2024, https://www.congreso.gob.pe) y Archivo Digital de la Legislación del Perú
  (https://www.leyes.congreso.gob.pe), retrieved 28 October 2026; earlier Congreso editions read through the
  Internet Archive (captures pinned in tools/parse.py).

They are official texts of the Republic of Peru. Decreto Legislativo 822 (Ley sobre el Derecho de Autor), article 9,
excludes official texts of a legislative, administrative or judicial nature from copyright protection.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised and degree signs after article numbers dropped; the Congreso's notes were
removed from the text and used only to rebuild earlier versions and to credit the amending law; and the versions were
arranged as git commits credited to the laws and the ruling that made each change. The wording of the law was not
changed. The Congreso de la República does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
